; teamchat: the SELinux policy the v2 team units need on an enforcing host.
;
; The units run their programs from /usr/local (bin_t) with NoNewPrivileges=yes, so no domain
; transition happens and they run as init_t. init_t may not connect to an ordinary unreserved
; port, so the TLS terminator could not reach its team's homeserver on loopback, and
; teamchat-admin could not reach it either.
;
; Each present team's declared port is labelled teamchat_port_t by play-teamchat.yml. The port
; type keeps the unreserved_port_type attribute, so every domain that could connect to the port
; before it was labelled still can, and init_t may bind and connect to these ports only: no
; other port is opened to it.
(type teamchat_port_t)
(roletype object_r teamchat_port_t)
(typeattributeset port_type (teamchat_port_t))
(typeattributeset unreserved_port_type (teamchat_port_t))
(allow init_t teamchat_port_t (tcp_socket (name_bind name_connect)))
